# The Eisenstein series E4 and the theta series of the eight-dimensional even unimodular lattice, which are the same
# function. A modular form of weight four is fixed by one coefficient sequence, and for E4 that sequence is one followed by
# two hundred forty times the cube divisor sums, so the number of lattice vectors of squared length two n is exactly two
# hundred forty times sigma-three of n. The cubes are the arithmetic underneath, and this file MODELS the cube by its
# GNOMON, the odd-shell increment that turns one cube into the next: the difference between consecutive cubes is three n
# squared plus three n plus one. It DEFINES the cube by accumulating those gnomons and PROVES that the accumulation is
# exactly n cubed, so the cube function is pinned by its increments. It then records, as machine-integer counts, the theta
# shell numbers as two hundred forty times the cube divisor sums. The gnomon closed form is proved for every n by the
# commutative-ring normalizer.

# The cube of n, built by accumulating gnomons: cube(0) = 0, and cube(n) = cube(n-1) + (3 m^2 + 3 m + 1) where m = n - 1,
# the increment from one cube to the next.
task cube
  take n, like natural-number
  like natural-number
  send back
    fork test
      hook test
        call is-equal
          read n
          code 0
      hook hold
        code 0
      hook miss
        call add
          call cube
            call subtract
              read n
              code 1
          call add
            call add
              call multiply
                code 3
                call multiply
                  call subtract
                    read n
                    code 1
                  call subtract
                    read n
                    code 1
              call multiply
                code 3
                call subtract
                  read n
                  code 1
            code 1

# THE GNOMON CLOSED FORM: accumulating the gnomons three m squared plus three m plus one gives exactly n cubed,
# cube(n) = n * n * n, for every n. So the cube function is determined by its shell increments, the discrete derivative of
# the cube. This is the cube arithmetic the theta series inherits. Proved for all n by the commutative-ring normalizer.
rule the-gnomons-accumulate-to-the-cube
  seat n, like natural-number
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call cube
        read n
      call multiply
        read n
        call multiply
          read n
          read n
  fold n

# THE THETA SHELL COUNTS as machine-integer facts: the number of eight-dimensional lattice vectors of squared length two n
# is two hundred forty times the cube divisor sum sigma-three of n. Shell one, the kissing number: 240 = 240 * 1.
hold theta-shell-one-is-two-hundred-forty
  call is-equal
    code 240
    call multiply
      code 240
      code 1

# Shell two, squared length four: 240 * sigma-three(2) = 240 * 9 = 2160.
hold theta-shell-two-is-two-thousand-one-hundred-sixty
  call is-equal
    code 2160
    call multiply
      code 240
      code 9

# Shell three, squared length six: 240 * sigma-three(3) = 240 * 28 = 6720.
hold theta-shell-three-is-six-thousand-seven-hundred-twenty
  call is-equal
    code 6720
    call multiply
      code 240
      code 28
